    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Minor-key harmony shifts with natural, harmonic, and melodic minor scales."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "natural-minor",
      "title": "Natural minor",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "i, ii°, III, iv, v, VI, VII. In Am: Am, Bdim, C, Dm, Em, F, G. v is minor — weaker cadence."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "harmonic-minor",
      "title": "Harmonic minor",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Raised 7th makes V major (E major in Am) with strong pull to i. III and VI provide modal pivots."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trad-practice",
      "title": "Trad practice",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Listen for raised 7th at cadences. Irish minor tunes blend aeolian and dorian without announcing which textbook scale they follow."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
